WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.773
Global navigation satellite systems, often shortened to G N S S, provide position, navigation,

00:00:05.773 --> 00:00:06.989
and timing services.

00:00:06.989 --> 00:00:09.015
GPS is one such system.

00:00:09.015 --> 00:00:12.256
Drones, vehicles, maps, communications, financial systems, power infrastructure,

00:00:12.256 --> 00:00:16.308
and many other technologies depend on satellite-derived position or time.

00:00:16.308 --> 00:00:21.576
Jamming is radio-frequency interference that degrades or blocks reception of weak satellite-navigation signals.

00:00:21.576 --> 00:00:24.818
It may cause lost lock, poor accuracy, warnings,

00:00:24.818 --> 00:00:28.059
or failure of features that depend on position.

00:00:28.059 --> 00:00:32.517
Interference can be intentional, accidental, local, or caused by equipment faults.

00:00:32.517 --> 00:00:39.000
Spoofing is deceptive signal manipulation intended to make a receiver calculate an incorrect position or time.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.078
A receiver may continue reporting a confident-looking solution even though that solution disagrees with reality.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:48.320
These definitions describe effects, not a field diagnosis.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.777
Poor sky view, reflected signals, urban canyons, antenna problems, receiver faults,

00:00:52.777 --> 00:00:57.235
compass interference, software issues, or stale maps can create similar symptoms.

00:00:57.235 --> 00:01:00.476
One unusual reading does not prove an attack.

00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:05.339
For drone operators, the immediate question is not who caused the anomaly.

00:01:05.339 --> 00:01:07.770
It is whether navigation, automation, logs,

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:12.227
and situational awareness remain trustworthy enough for safe flight and recovery.

00:01:12.227 --> 00:01:14.253
This course is defensive only.

00:01:14.253 --> 00:01:17.090
Never transmit interference or deceptive navigation signals.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:20.737
The goal is to understand dependencies, recognize suspicious behavior,

00:01:20.737 --> 00:01:25.194
reduce reliance on uncertain automation, protect people and property, preserve evidence,

00:01:25.194 --> 00:01:27.220
and report through appropriate channels.
